        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": "Title",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What is in the standard library documentation?",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "First of all, The Rust Standard Library is divided into a number of focused",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "modules, ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "all listed further down this page",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "#modules"
            },
            {
              "text": ". These modules are",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "the bedrock upon which all of Rust is forged, and they have mighty names",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "like ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "std::slice",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "path": "alloc::slice"
            },
            {
              "text": " and ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "std::cmp",
              "style": "InlineCode",
              "path": "core::cmp"
            },
            {
              "text": ". Modules' documentation typically",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "includes an overview of the module along with examples, and are a smart",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "place to start familiarizing yourself with the library.",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Second, implicit methods on ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "primitive types",
              "style": "Plain",
              "url": "../book/ch03-02-data-types.html"
            },
            {
              "text": " are documented here. This can",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": " ",
              "style": "Plain"
            },
            {
              "text": "be a source of confusion for two reasons:",
              "style": "Plain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "While primitives are implemented by the compiler, the standard library",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " ",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "implements methods directly on the primitive types (and it is the only",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " ",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "library that does so), which are ",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "documented in the section on",
                      "style": "Plain",
                      "url": "#primitives"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " ",
                      "style": "Plain",
                      "url": "#primitives"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "primitives",
                      "style": "Plain",
                      "url": "#primitives"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": ".",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "The standard library exports many modules ",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "with the same name as",
                      "style": "Emphasis"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " ",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "primitive types",
                      "style": "Emphasis"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": ". These define additional items related to the primitive",
                      "style": "Plain"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " ",
